---
import SiteLayout from '../components/SiteLayout.astro';
import { places, industries } from '../lib/catalog.mjs';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site.mjs';
import coverage from '../data/coverage.json';
---
<SiteLayout title="Place and business data sources | AdSquirrel" description="Provenance, coverage and limitations of the Kerala place directory and business category taxonomy used by AdSquirrel." canonical={`${SITE.url}/data-sources/`}>
  <main id="main" class="directory-page"><div class="directory-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A CLEARER VIEW</p><h1>Local names.<br /><em>Open sources.</em></h1><p>Our directory currently includes {places.length.toLocaleString('en-IN')} Kerala place records and {industries.length} practical business categories.</p></div>
  <section class="directory-group"><h2>What our place directory represents</h2><p>Place names are drawn from LGD-derived administrative records and named OpenStreetMap place nodes. This build includes {coverage.counts.lgdVillageSourceRows.toLocaleString('en-IN')} source village rows, {coverage.counts.lgdTaluks} taluks and {coverage.counts.osmSourceNodes.toLocaleString('en-IN')} source OpenStreetMap nodes before merging overlapping names. Administrative villages, neighbourhoods and everyday place names do not always have the same boundaries or spelling. Records retain source and district information; repeated names are disambiguated by their URL.</p><p>The LGD-derived records use the 25 September 2026 snapshot distributed in the pinned village-finder release. The OpenStreetMap place snapshot is dated 3 November 2026. Neither is a live Google Maps export.</p><p><a href="https://lgdirectory.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Local Government Directory, Government of India — Government Open Data License India ↗</a></p><p><a href="https://github.com/mchittineni/india-village-finder/releases/tag/v1.5.19" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pinned LGD-derived village dataset release ↗</a></p><p><a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">© OpenStreetMap contributors — Open Database License ↗</a></p><p><a href="/api/coverage.json">Read the full source, license and coverage manifest (JSON) ↗</a></p></section>
  <section class="directory-group"><h2>Business categories</h2><p>The industry directory is a practical marketing taxonomy informed by the National Industrial Classification and business activity categories. The complete imported taxonomy contains {coverage.counts.nicRecords.toLocaleString('en-IN')} division, group, class and subclass records across NIC 2008 and NIC 2025. It is not an official register of every Kerala business, nor evidence that AdSquirrel has worked with a particular category.</p><p><a href="https://www.mospi.gov.in/national-industrial-classification" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Industrial Classification, Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation ↗</a></p><p><a href="/api/taxonomy.json">Explore the full imported NIC taxonomy and sources (JSON) ↗</a></p></section>
  <section class="directory-group"><h2>Reuse and attribution</h2><p>The combined place database is offered under the Open Database License. It contains information from the Local Government Directory under Government Open Data License India and © OpenStreetMap contributors. This dataset license does not apply to the website’s original code, design or marketing copy.</p><p><a href="/api/places.json">Download the complete derived place database (JSON) ↗</a></p></section>
  <section class="directory-group"><h2>Coverage and corrections</h2><p>No source can guarantee every hamlet, informal name, newly developed locality or alternate transliteration. We do not claim complete coverage. A locality page means that we offer services to that area; our stated physical office remains in Kalamassery.</p><p>Found a missing place or incorrect district? Send the name and a reliable source to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p></section></main>
</SiteLayout>
